# The module's SDO is pulled to ground, so the sketch calls begin(0x76). The compensated
# print is the world: 20.00 °C exactly, and 101325 Pa within a few hundredths, which prints
# as 101325.02. The sheet allows 1 °C and 1 hPa. The stock Adafruit_BMP280 example calls
# setSampling() after begin() already entered normal mode, so the config write is ignored
# and warns config_in_normal (BST-BMP280-DS001 §4.3.5).
open
step 1ms
set temperature 20
set pressure 101325
step --until serial contains " Pa" --timeout 2s
step 20ms
expect serial contains "Temperature = 20.00"
expect serial contains "Pressure = 101325.02"
expect @mod.VCC >= 1.71V
expect @mod.VCC <= 3.6V
expect diagnostics contains "warning[chip.protocol]"
expect diagnostics contains "config_in_normal"
